{"term":"retirement","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:7e36a432bc848c5941","definition":"An act of retiring; withdrawal.","example":"After dinner there was the peaceful pipe that Tulloch had forecast, and mutual reminiscences until the long clock in the corner, striking the smallest hour of the morning, prompted Tulloch to suggest retirement.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["departure","withdrawment"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["deed of retirement","early retirement","early retirement pensioner","microretirement","miniretirement","nonretirement","postretirement","preretirement","protirement","retirement annuity contract","retirement annuity plan","retirement community","retirement home","retirement syndrome","retirement village","semiretirement","unretirement"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retirement#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cd3c69d1bb5807cdb8","definition":"The state of being retired; seclusion.","example":"The heir to the throne of Bogota […] had to undergo a rigorous training from his infancy: he lived in complete retirement in a temple, where he might not see the sun nor eat salt nor converse with a woman: he was surrounded by guards who observed his conduct and noted all his actions.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["privacy","seclusion","solitude"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["deed of retirement","early retirement","early retirement pensioner","microretirement","miniretirement","nonretirement","postretirement","preretirement","protirement","retirement annuity contract","retirement annuity plan","retirement community","retirement home","retirement syndrome","retirement village","semiretirement","unretirement"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retirement#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:17b598459626aca168","definition":"A place of seclusion or privacy; a retreat.","example":"When her mother frowned, and her friend looked cool, she would steal to this retirement, where human foot seldom trod […].","pos":"noun","synonyms":["retreat"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["deed of retirement","early retirement","early retirement pensioner","microretirement","miniretirement","nonretirement","postretirement","preretirement","protirement","retirement annuity contract","retirement annuity plan","retirement community","retirement home","retirement syndrome","retirement village","semiretirement","unretirement"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retirement#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7619cfd7f2608cb452","definition":"The state of having permanently left one's employment, now especially at reaching pensionable age; the portion of one's life after retiring from one's career.","example":"\"I tried retirement ten years ago. Didn't think much of it. Complete waste of time. So I gave it up after two weeks.\"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["deed of retirement","early retirement","early retirement pensioner","microretirement","miniretirement","nonretirement","postretirement","preretirement","protirement","retirement annuity contract","retirement annuity plan","retirement community","retirement home","retirement syndrome","retirement village","semiretirement","unretirement"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retirement#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3cfe668ca87823ce61","definition":"The act of leaving